    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T13:42:09Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/1050-developed-band-exit · PR #1210 · pinned by `lift_swept::tests::a_rapid_landing_on_a_sub_cell_wall_strip_is_refused`, `lift_swept::tests::a_disc_is_covered_on_the_cut_and_not_a_hair_past_it`, `lift_tests::a_piece_starting_where_the_tool_stands_is_ridden_on_to`, `adaptive_hsm::hsm_report_full_resolution` · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: the return over the retract plane (`LinkLaw::high`, not the hop) read its landing on the planner's cell bitmap; a 0.075 mm wall strip between two rows of cell centers was invisible to it. Fix: the plan keeps the segments its pieces cut and the rapid lands only where the whole footprint is proved swept (quadtree on exact distances, r - 12.5 um, the verifier's own reading of arcs). The slot's \"4 descents\" was a second fault: a retract and plunge on one spot between two abutting pieces, now ridden on. Narrow slot: verifier silent, 2 descents, 0 hops. Decision: `docs/decisions/1169-landing-on-swept-stock.md`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
